These are completely different.

10. How notify() Works

Suppose

Wait Set
↓
Thread-A

Thread-B

Current owner executes
lock.notify();

JVM moves one thread

Wait Set
↓
Entry Set / Runnable to compete for the monitor

The notified thread is eligible to reacquire the monitor, but it does not own it yet.

Interview Note: Conceptually, the thread leaves the Wait Set. It must compete to reacquire the monitor before continuing. Different JVM implementations may describe this transition slightly differently internally, but the key idea is that notify() does not immediately give the thread the lock.

